      "title": "Ukraine hit by deadly Russian strikes as ‘thanks’ for Trump diesel deal, Zelenskyy says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/ukraine-russia-strikes-war-trump-diesel-deal-zelenskyy",
      "description": "<p>Ukrainian president says money from fuel sales will intensify war as European leaders reiterate support for Kyiv</p><p>Russia launched deadly strikes on civilians in Ukraine as “thanks” for a deal cut by Donald Trump with Vladimir Putin to buy large quantities of Russian diesel, Volodymyr Zelenskyy has said, accusing Washington of helping fund Moscow’s war.</p><p>The Ukrainian president has expressed repeated outrage at the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/09/trump-putin-russian-diesel-ukraine\">agreement announced by Trump</a> on Friday, which the US president said was needed to reduce diesel prices, and comes ahead of November midterm elections in which fuel costs are a key voter issue.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/10/ukraine-russia-strikes-war-trump-diesel-deal-zelenskyy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
